      "db_id": 17592186166867,
      "id": "53a1649d-4279-5b7c-839c-728f333b2c3f",
      "title": "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parabola"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "9a56f0b0-10bf-5ed0-8272-89f6e9836f8b",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/edb-math/repairs/2026-10-28-topic-audit-3/published-probe/17592186166867/1066c0b7c664ee8952ac5f4489080254e867baa352278074b2e31c1a608ea711.png)\n\nThe parabola shown above has equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=36x.\n$$\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "44db76b2-1a25-5b40-a1ec-c45f675173c5",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "6ee56850-e9ca-5ccf-a5a3-7ccaec82949c",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{18}{y}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "6ee56850-e9ca-5ccf-a5a3-7ccaec82949c"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "The equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=36x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(36x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =36 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{18}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy"
    },
